2026-09-23 — B02 compared-value instruction selection; original B02 stays OPEN.

RED: compared_value_csel has one expected failing shape assertion, two passing
controls and zero Rust compilation errors: no CSEL is selected for the complete
comparison/extension/negated-mask/XOR chain.

GREEN: the shared MIR lowerer selects existing CMP/CSEL only for the contiguous
single-use 32/64-bit chain. The comparison's already-evaluated inputs are the
two choices, optionally reversed. Nonzero masks, changed dependencies, another
consumer, intervening instructions, narrower/128-bit types and symbolic-address
operands keep ordinary lowering. All source guards, memory/volatile/atomic
observations and local SSA bindings remain. Flags have one adjacent consumer.
No new IR operation, verifier relaxation, unchecked profile or EqSat rule.
EvoMIR 0.36 records this bounded selection, not a new language permission.

Three MIR tests pass: 96 matched shape/allocation/round-trip cases, 600 exact
execution comparisons (zero, one, signed extrema and all-ones), and eight
nonmatching chains. Seven CLI tests pass both C-HIR/EvoIR O0/O2 and machine
controls, including high-bit signed/unsigned selection, surrounding effects,
unselected arms and retained E3001/E3004/E3009/E3011 diagnostics.
Two C fixtures x GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC x O0/O2 = 12 native PASS in the sealed
linux/arm64 image with networking disabled. Raw compiler warnings are retained.

The unchanged LLVM LARGE floyd-warshall is rebuilt via its existing projector,
source hash, original argv, sysroot and output comparison contract. The core
shrinks from 108 to 102 instructions, but the original program still reaches
60 seconds, exits 124, and timeit kills its monitored process. This is TIMEOUT,
not an output PASS. Both core versions in the original binary get CSEL.
The rebuilt release emits byte-identical original assembly to the tested debug
compiler. No kernel Image or full benchmark receipt inherits this improvement.

Affected gate against 0ac63cd: 980 PASS, zero FAIL, four historical ignored,
119 result groups in evocc, evocc-mir, evocc-policy, evocc-proofcheck and
evocc-randgate. Clippy --all-targets -D warnings and workspace fmt PASS.
The four ignored standing native/extended campaigns remain ignored, not passes.
Status is regenerated; diff and renderer checks pass.

